Usage: ateam <command>

agent-teams workspace CLI

Flags:
  -h, --help    Show context-sensitive help.

Commands:
  reopen <id>
    Reopen a closed initiative.

  register --title=STRING --file=STRING
    Register a new initiative from a body file.

  note --file=STRING <id>
    Add a note to an initiative.

  gate <id> [flags]
    Add a gate (human-review request) to an initiative.

  clear-gate <id> [flags]
    Clear the human-review gate on an initiative.

  handoff <id> [flags]
    Declare (or clear) that the human is done looking at an initiative; it's on
    the team for external review.

  learn <role> <slug> [flags]
    Store a memory for a role.

  close <id> [flags]
    Close an initiative.

  pull [flags]
    Pull the remote beads database (dolt pull).

  sync
    Pull then push the beads database (bounded non-ff retry).

  forget <role> <slug>
    Delete a role memory by key.

  applied <role> <slug>
    Record an applied-signal for a role's learning (bumps count + last_applied).

  condense <role>
    Emit a structured memory packet for a role.

  fresh-drain <role>
    Drain fresh: memories to cold for a role.

  update-description --file=STRING <id>
    Update an initiative's description from a file.

  condense-lock <action>
    Acquire or release the advisory condense lock.

  condense-check [<role>] [flags]
    Compute the condense fire/skip verdict for one role or all roles
    (read-only).

  cost <initiative-id> [flags]
    Report estimated token cost for an initiative.

  ws
    Print the workspace home path.

  list
    List open initiatives.

  list-json [flags]
    List initiatives as JSON, each with its parsed routing fields.

  human-list
    List gated beads awaiting human input.

  show <id>
    Show details for an initiative.

  learnings <role>
    Print role memories (hot+fresh, or all).

  instructions <role>
    Print a role's machine-local human-authored instructions file, if any.

  recall <role> <query>
    Search role memories by tokenized query, ranked by matched terms.

  prime
    Print cross-project user preferences.

  roles
    List role namespaces present in workspace memories.

  memories-json
    List all role memories as JSON with tier + applied signal.

  audit
    Audit global workspace for leaked work beads.

  resume-match <worktree-path>
    Find the open initiative whose worktree is EXACTLY this path (no ancestor
    matching).

  resume-match-closed <worktree-path>
    Find the most-recently-closed initiative whose worktree is EXACTLY this path
    (no ancestor matching).

  resolve-initiative <path> [flags]
    Find the open initiative owning this path, ancestor-or-self (the worktree
    root or any subdirectory of it).

  hook-scan [<path>] [flags]
    Resolve a path to its owning initiative and report unread mail, from one
    Dolt open.

  new-initiative <directory> [<dri-arg> ...]
    Spawn a background DRI session in <directory>.

  dispatch --problem=STRING [flags]
    Create a worktree, register an initiative, and optionally launch a DRI
    session.

  resume [<id>] [flags]
    Re-launch a background DRI session for an existing initiative.

  runtime check <runtime> [flags]
    Check whether a runtime is available.

  runtime open <runtime>
    Open a runtime's native session view.

  setup codex [flags]
    Install and verify Codex-specific agent-teams components.

  worktree-setup [<wtPath>]
    Run repo-specific worktree-setup hook for the given worktree.

  mail send <recipient-initiative-id> [flags]
    Send a message to a recipient initiative.

  mail inbox [flags]
    Read and consume unread messages for this initiative.

  mail list [flags]
    List recent cross-initiative mail (all statuses, including closed).

  mail close <id>
    Close a message bead.

  mail purge [flags]
    Permanently delete old closed message beads.

  mail follow [flags]
    On a hosted workspace, start the per-host follower that rings local
    initiatives' doorbells from the events journal.

  mail bridge [flags]
    Deliver hosted bridge:laptop mail from cloud_home to this machine (--once
    for one pass).

  route-pr-event --repo=STRING --pr-number=INT --head-branch=STRING --transition=PR-TRANSITION --body-file=STRING [flags]
    Route a PR event to an owning initiative.

  execution-status
    Emit JSON array of open initiatives with execution state.

  hung-scan
    Emit JSON array of open initiatives classified for hung-session detection.

  watchers
    Show watcher state for all open initiatives.

  reap-orphans
    Stop background sessions whose worktree cwd no longer exists.

  reap [<target>] [flags]
    Tear down closed review sessions past grace (scan mode, what pr-shepherd
    calls every tick) or one target right now (one-off mode); see reap-orphans
    for stop-only cwd-missing cleanup.

  notify --file=STRING <id> [flags]
    Send a message to a human via the configured transport.

  relay
    Long-poll the configured transport and relay human replies to the Steward.

  steward init
    Create the Steward session directory and marker file.

  steward start [flags]
    Init, then singleton/orphan-watcher pre-flight checks, then launch the
    Steward's background session.

  steward ledger record --category=STRING --initiative=STRING --recommendation=STRING --verdict=STRING [flags]
    Append one decision to the Steward's ledger.

  steward ledger stats [flags]
    Report per-category accept/correct counts from the ledger.

  steward ledger recall <category> [flags]
    Recall recent decisions for one category (most recent first).

  steward ledger self --since=STRING [flags]
    List the steward's self-decisions since a time, with their reviews.

  steward ledger seed [flags]
    Copy the local ledger file into the hosted ledger store (cloud_home);
    never overwrites.

  steward startup
    Print the steward's startup text: ledger rules, ledger stats, outsider
    rules, learnings. Prints all of it or nothing.

  steward remove [flags]
    De-steward this machine: remove the session dir and doorbell
    (ledger/briefing kept unless --purge).

  tie-session [<initiative-id>] [flags]
    Tie this session's id to its initiative (self-registration).

  sent [flags]
    Read back the audit log of messages sent to the human (who sent what, when).

  spawn-check [flags]
    Witness whether a named teammate spawn actually attached its role definition
    (reads the harness's own subagent sidecar).

  preflight [flags]
    Launch a live probe session and verify the agent-teams role/model/spawn
    plumbing end to end.

  pr add <initiative-id> <pr-url>
    Record a GitHub PR URL on an initiative's pr rail.

  pr context <initiative-id> [flags]
    Print the multi-PR context block for an initiative
    (docs/outsider-requests.md).

  cloud-boot start [flags]
    Adopt the run's initiative, launch the DRI under tmux, and park (exit 75)
    when it goes idle.

  cloud-boot resume [flags]
    Relaunch the parked DRI session with the Dispatcher wake event as its
    prompt.

  live-test file --worktree=STRING --scope=STRING --items-file=STRING [flags]
    File a live-test bead (--job picks the UI or API job) for a pushed branch in
    the Dispatcher's beads database; prints the bead id.

  live-test wait --out=STRING <bead-id> [flags]
    Wait up to --timeout for the bead's verdict, then write it and its evidence
    (screenshots or transcript.json) under --out. Exit 7 means the job type's
    evidence is missing. Exit 8 means the Socotra tenant pool is full: the
    POOL_FULL line is printed to stderr and written to failure.md; nothing ran,
    retry later.

  live-test watch <bead-id> [flags]
    Watch a live-test bead and mail its stop events (question, blocked, done,
    failed, expired) to the initiative.

  live-test reply <bead-id> [flags]
    Answer the tester's question on a live-test bead; prints '<id> <status>'.

  page template [flags]
    Print the shared plan-page kit (HTML); works anywhere. --out writes it to a
    file.

  page image <file> [flags]
    Print a <figure> snippet that embeds an image file as a data: URI; works
    anywhere.

  page publish <file> [flags]
    Publish an HTML file as a Dispatcher page (cloud run only); prints the page
    URL.

  learnings-seed [flags]
    Copy local role, user, and steward learnings (all tiers; per-machine
    steward:topics:<host> records stay local) into the hosted learnings store
    (cloud_home); never overwrites, and skips a key whose role and slug already
    exist hosted under any tier.

Run "ateam <command> --help" for more information on a command.
